<Layout title="Home">
  <div class="pill-row">
    <p class="pill">PhD in Bioengineering &middot; UC Berkeley/UCSF</p>
    <p class="pill">Major: Biomaterials &amp; Tissue Regeneration</p>
    <p class="pill">Minor: Cell, Developmental, and Tissue Biology</p>
  </div>
  <h1>Morgan R. Pfaff</h1>
  <p class="tagline">Bioengineer</p>
  <p>
    Hi, I'm Morgan! I completed my PhD in the joint UC Berkeley/UCSF
    Bioengineering program, engineering hyaluronic acid hydrogels in Dr.
    Kevin Healy's lab to help the body regenerate tissue after complex
    soft tissue injuries. Outside the lab, I volunteer with Food Not
    Bombs East Bay and love talking with anyone who wants to chase their
    own passion in STEM.
  </p>
  <div class="home-cta">
    <a class="btn" href="/about/">More About Me</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/projects/">See My Work</a>
  </div>
  <img
    src="/morgan-nu-portrait-hq.jpg"
    alt="Portrait of Morgan R. Pfaff outdoors on Northeastern's campus"
    class="card-img home-photo"
  />
  <p class="photo-credit">Photo by Matthew Modoono/Northeastern University</p>
</Layout>
